-- == Tutorial == (Dorn coaches you through four rounds)
L["Welcome to the table! I'm Dorn, and I'll show you how this works before we play for real. Each column is a lane. In combat every unit strikes the enemy unit straight across from it, or the enemy's Morale if nothing is there. You have 1 Supply to spend. Play your |cffffffffKobold Vermin|r in |cffffffffyour lane 2|r (the bottom row), then press Lock In."] = "Welcome to the table! I'm Dorn, and I'll show you how this works before we play for real. Each column is a lane. In combat every unit strikes the enemy unit straight across from it, or the enemy's Morale if nothing is there. You have 1 Supply to spend. Play your |cffffffffKobold Vermin|r in |cffffffffyour lane 2|r (the bottom row), then press Lock In."   -- round 1, while you plan
L["We both reveal at the same time. Watch where my unit goes."] = "We both reveal at the same time. Watch where my unit goes."   -- round 1, while it plays out
L["Your Kobold had nothing across from it, so it hit my Morale for 1. Mine was in lane 4 with nothing across, so it hit yours. A unit with nothing across keeps doing that every round. Whoever runs out of Morale loses."] = "Your Kobold had nothing across from it, so it hit my Morale for 1. Mine was in lane 4 with nothing across, so it hit yours. A unit with nothing across keeps doing that every round. Whoever runs out of Morale loses."   -- round 1, afterwards
L["My Kobold in lane 4 will keep hitting you. Block it: put your |cffffffffDefias Thug|r in |cffffffffyour lane 4|r, right across from it. The marker between the rows shows what each lane will do; it turns from a red arrow into crossed swords."] = "My Kobold in lane 4 will keep hitting you. Block it: put your |cffffffffDefias Thug|r in |cffffffffyour lane 4|r, right across from it. The marker between the rows shows what each lane will do; it turns from a red arrow into crossed swords."   -- round 2, while you plan
L["Units that face each other fight. Both strike at the same time."] = "Units that face each other fight. Both strike at the same time."   -- round 2, while it plays out
L["Blocked! Your Thug destroyed my Kobold. Damage stays on a unit until it dies, so a battered unit is easy to finish off. My Plainstrider's Arrive effect gave me some Morale back when it came in."] = "Blocked! Your Thug destroyed my Kobold. Damage stays on a unit until it dies, so a battered unit is easy to finish off. My Plainstrider's Arrive effect gave me some Morale back when it came in."   -- round 2, afterwards
L["Tactics are different: they go off after both sides' new units arrive, so a tactic aimed at an empty lane hits whatever lands there. Psst, I'm about to put a beast in lane 3. Cast |cffffffffFireball|r at |cffffffffmy lane 3|r (the top row), and play your |cffffffffYoung Wolf|r in |cffffffffyour lane 1|r."] = "Tactics are different: they go off after both sides' new units arrive, so a tactic aimed at an empty lane hits whatever lands there. Psst, I'm about to put a beast in lane 3. Cast |cffffffffFireball|r at |cffffffffmy lane 3|r (the top row), and play your |cffffffffYoung Wolf|r in |cffffffffyour lane 1|r."   -- round 3, while you plan
L["Watch the order: new units arrive first, then tactics, then combat."] = "Watch the order: new units arrive first, then tactics, then combat."   -- round 3, while it plays out
L["See that? My Lashtail arrived in lane 3 and your Fireball hit it before it could strike. Usually you won't know where I'll play. Guessing right is half the game."] = "See that? My Lashtail arrived in lane 3 and your Fireball hit it before it could strike. Usually you won't know where I'll play. Guessing right is half the game."   -- round 3, afterwards
L["You can't block every lane. A unit with |cff7fbfffGuard|r covers the lanes beside it: an enemy with nothing across that's next to your Guard strikes the Guard instead of your Morale. Play your |cffffffffGrizzled Black Bear|r in |cffffffffyour lane 2|r."] = "You can't block every lane. A unit with |cff7fbfffGuard|r covers the lanes beside it: an enemy with nothing across that's next to your Guard strikes the Guard instead of your Morale. Play your |cffffffffGrizzled Black Bear|r in |cffffffffyour lane 2|r."   -- round 4, while you plan
L["Keep an eye on lane 3."] = "Keep an eye on lane 3."   -- round 4, while it plays out
L["My Boar had nothing across in lane 3, but your Bear stepped in and took the hit, so your Morale is safe. Keywords like Guard are printed on the card. Hover any card to see what they do."] = "My Boar had nothing across in lane 3, but your Bear stepped in and took the hit, so your Morale is safe. Keywords like Guard are printed on the card. Hover any card to see what they do."   -- round 4, afterwards
L["That's the basics. From here on I play for real. Win this one and you're ready for the circuit. Hover the markers between the rows to see what each lane will do; the Guide tab explains the rest."] = "That's the basics. From here on I play for real. Win this one and you're ready for the circuit. Hover the markers between the rows to see what each lane will do; the Guide tab explains the rest."   -- after round 4

