-- == UI/Guide.lua ==
L["The goal"] = "The goal"
L["You and your opponent each start with |cffffffff12 Morale|r. Bring theirs to 0, or have more than they do when round 8 ends."] = "You and your opponent each start with |cffffffff12 Morale|r. Bring theirs to 0, or have more than they do when round 8 ends."
L["Both at once"] = "Both at once"
L["Every round you both plan in secret and lock in. Then both plans are revealed together and the round plays out."] = "Every round you both plan in secret and lock in. Then both plans are revealed together and the round plays out."
L["Each round you get Supply to spend on cards: 1 in round 1, 2 in round 2, and so on up to 6. Supply you don't spend is lost. You draw a card at the start of every round. The draws in rounds 1 to 3 never cost more than that round's Supply (round 1's is always a unit), so there's always something to play."] = "Each round you get Supply to spend on cards: 1 in round 1, 2 in round 2, and so on up to 6. Supply you don't spend is lost. You draw a card at the start of every round. The draws in rounds 1 to 3 never cost more than that round's Supply (round 1's is always a unit), so there's always something to play."
L["Lanes"] = "Lanes"
L["The board has four lanes: the columns. Your units go in the bottom row, theirs in the top row. In combat each unit strikes the enemy unit straight across from it. If nothing is across from it, it strikes the enemy's |cffffffffMorale|r instead."] = "The board has four lanes: the columns. Your units go in the bottom row, theirs in the top row. In combat each unit strikes the enemy unit straight across from it. If nothing is across from it, it strikes the enemy's |cffffffffMorale|r instead."
L["Put units across from theirs to block them, and in open lanes to hit their Morale. Damage on a unit stays until it dies."] = "Put units across from theirs to block them, and in open lanes to hit their Morale. Damage on a unit stays until it dies."
L["While you plan, the markers between the rows show what each lane will do if your opponent plays nothing new. Hover one for the details."] = "While you plan, the markers between the rows show what each lane will do if your opponent plays nothing new. Hover one for the details."
L["A round, step by step"] = "A round, step by step"
L["|cffffffff1. Start.|r Both players draw a card and get their Supply. Round start effects happen."] = "|cffffffff1. Start.|r Both players draw a card and get their Supply. Round start effects happen."
L["|cffffffff2. Plan.|r Click a card in your hand, then where it goes (or drag it there). A unit or a trap goes in one of your empty lanes. A tactic targets an enemy lane, one of your units, or nothing. Right-click a planned card to take it back. Lock In when you're ready."] = "|cffffffff2. Plan.|r Click a card in your hand, then where it goes (or drag it there). A unit or a trap goes in one of your empty lanes. A tactic targets an enemy lane, one of your units, or nothing. Right-click a planned card to take it back. Lock In when you're ready."
L["|cffffffff3. Reveal.|r Both plans are shown. All the new units arrive in their lanes and traps are set face down, then the Arrive effects happen."] = "|cffffffff3. Reveal.|r Both plans are shown. All the new units arrive in their lanes and traps are set face down, then the Arrive effects happen."
L["|cffffffff4. Tactics.|r Each tactic goes off, the player with |cffffffffinitiative|r first (initiative swaps every round). Because tactics come after the units arrive, a tactic aimed at an empty enemy lane hits whatever was just played there."] = "|cffffffff4. Tactics.|r Each tactic goes off, the player with |cffffffffinitiative|r first (initiative swaps every round). Because tactics come after the units arrive, a tactic aimed at an empty enemy lane hits whatever was just played there."
L["|cffffffff5. Combat.|r Swift units strike first, all at once. Then every other unit strikes, all at once. A strike into an empty lane with a trap in it springs the trap. After each of those two steps, units with no health left die and their Fallen effects happen."] = "|cffffffff5. Combat.|r Swift units strike first, all at once. Then every other unit strikes, all at once. A strike into an empty lane with a trap in it springs the trap. After each of those two steps, units with no health left die and their Fallen effects happen."
L["|cffffffff6. End.|r Regenerate units heal, and effects that last \"this round\" wear off. If either player's Morale is 0 or less, or it was round 8, the game is over."] = "|cffffffff6. End.|r Regenerate units heal, and effects that last \"this round\" wear off. If either player's Morale is 0 or less, or it was round 8, the game is over."
L["Your hand holds up to 7 cards. A card drawn into a full hand is lost."] = "Your hand holds up to 7 cards. A card drawn into a full hand is lost."
L["Words on the cards"] = "Words on the cards"
L["|cffffffffArrive:|r happens when the unit is played, once both sides' new units are on the board."] = "|cffffffffArrive:|r happens when the unit is played, once both sides' new units are on the board."
L["|cffffffffFallen:|r happens when the unit dies."] = "|cffffffffFallen:|r happens when the unit dies."
L["|cffffffffRound start:|r happens at the start of every round while the unit is on the board."] = "|cffffffffRound start:|r happens at the start of every round while the unit is on the board."
L["|cffffffffFrozen:|r a frozen unit doesn't strike this round."] = "|cffffffffFrozen:|r a frozen unit doesn't strike this round."
L["Tactics"] = "Tactics"
L["A tactic is played once, then it's gone. Its type line says what it targets:"] = "A tactic is played once, then it's gone. Its type line says what it targets:"
L["|cffffffffTactic: enemy lane|r  pick a lane in the top row. It hits the unit there after the reveal; some tactics do something else if the lane is empty (Fireball hits Morale instead)."] = "|cffffffffTactic: enemy lane|r  pick a lane in the top row. It hits the unit there after the reveal; some tactics do something else if the lane is empty (Fireball hits Morale instead)."
L["|cffffffffTactic: your unit|r  pick one of your units, or a lane you're playing a unit into this round."] = "|cffffffffTactic: your unit|r  pick one of your units, or a lane you're playing a unit into this round."
L["|cffffffffTactic|r  no target needed."] = "|cffffffffTactic|r  no target needed."
L["|cffffffffItems|r (potions, bombs, weapons) are tactics too and play the same way, with a leather frame and \"Item\" on the type line. Gear stays on the unit, like Shield Wall."] = "|cffffffffItems|r (potions, bombs, weapons) are tactics too and play the same way, with a leather frame and \"Item\" on the type line. Gear stays on the unit, like Shield Wall."
L["|cffffffffTraps|r have a green frame and go face down in your own empty lanes. The Traps page explains them."] = "|cffffffffTraps|r have a green frame and go face down in your own empty lanes. The Traps page explains them."
L["Tribes"] = "Tribes"
L["Every unit belongs to a tribe: Beasts, Humanoids, Murlocs, Undead, Defias or Dragonkin. Some cards get stronger with others of their tribe beside them or in play. A card's tribe is on the line under its name."] = "Every unit belongs to a tribe: Beasts, Humanoids, Murlocs, Undead, Defias or Dragonkin. Some cards get stronger with others of their tribe beside them or in play. A card's tribe is on the line under its name."
L["Units of different tribes can have the same stats: on their own they play the same, and their tribe decides which cards count them. Point at a card that counts a tribe and the units it counts light up."] = "Units of different tribes can have the same stats: on their own they play the same, and their tribe decides which cards count them. Point at a card that counts a tribe and the units it counts light up."
L["The Cards tab can filter by tribe. One of every card of a tribe earns a Windfall pack."] = "The Cards tab can filter by tribe. One of every card of a tribe earns a Windfall pack."
L["Summoned units"] = "Summoned units"
L["Some cards bring extra units onto the board, like Hogger's Riverpaw Runts. They aren't part of any deck."] = "Some cards bring extra units onto the board, like Hogger's Riverpaw Runts. They aren't part of any deck."
L["A trap is a card you set face down in one of your empty lanes, as you would play a unit there. Your opponent sees that you have a trap set (a count by your Morale), but not which one or where."] = "A trap is a card you set face down in one of your empty lanes, as you would play a unit there. Your opponent sees that you have a trap set (a count by your Morale), but not which one or where."
L["It springs when an enemy unit strikes into that lane: the strike stops there and never reaches your Morale, the trap turns face up and does what it says, and then it's gone."] = "It springs when an enemy unit strikes into that lane: the strike stops there and never reaches your Morale, the trap turns face up and does what it says, and then it's gone."
L["Good to know"] = "Good to know"
L["Set one across from a unit that's hitting your Morale and it springs this round."] = "Set one across from a unit that's hitting your Morale and it springs this round."
L["Ranged units shoot over traps. A frozen unit, or one with no attack, doesn't strike, so it springs nothing."] = "Ranged units shoot over traps. A frozen unit, or one with no attack, doesn't strike, so it springs nothing."
L["Pierce doesn't carry on past a trap, and Drain gets nothing from it. Cleave still hits the units beside it."] = "Pierce doesn't carry on past a trap, and Drain gets nothing from it. Cleave still hits the units beside it."
L["A trap comes before a Guard next door. Tactics treat a trapped lane as empty: Fireball hits Morale and leaves the trap alone."] = "A trap comes before a Guard next door. Tactics treat a trapped lane as empty: Fireball hits Morale and leaves the trap alone."
L["Your units can't go in a lane with your trap, and summoned units skip it, which can give it away: a Hogger beside it leaves that lane empty. A unit a trap brings in arrives after combat, so it doesn't strike that round."] = "Your units can't go in a lane with your trap, and summoned units skip it, which can give it away: a Hogger beside it leaves that lane empty. A unit a trap brings in arrives after combat, so it doesn't strike that round."
L["Traps aren't units, so they don't count for the tiebreak. Any still face down when the game ends are shown on the end screen."] = "Traps aren't units, so they don't count for the tiebreak. Any still face down when the game ends are shown on the end screen."
